CREATED-BY: DXLog.net v2.6.15
SOAPBOX: 3 operators effort operating with 2 radios, (run & in-band),
SOAPBOX: one PC + 2 Keyboards (kind of SO2R setup). It worked as used to
SOAPBOX: since some years, but having 2 people dealing keys on two
SOAPBOX: keyboards on one PC and one Log brings to unexpected key
SOAPBOX: combinations... at some point the PC screen flipped upside-down...
SOAPBOX: and we kept running like this for some minutes, until it was time
SOAPBOX: to hold CQ and fix the issue. We had fun for this, but the fun was
SOAPBOX: compensated by terrible band conditions which
SOAPBOX: I have no memory in the past.
SOAPBOX: This year we managed to hear almost everyone, including
SOAPBOX: PP5JR coming strong for long time on Saturday morning, but
SOAPBOX: the best we got was some "?"... No way to be listened by
SOAPBOX: Dave K5GN calling lonely, and others from AZ, same for
SOAPBOX: some other (normally easy) stn in the east coast.
SOAPBOX: Surprisingly we were called by K7NJ from UT just before
SOAPBOX: our sunrise on Sat. We hoped for something more from Central
SOAPBOX: US like TX, IL, IN, ... but nothing happened :(
SOAPBOX: We managed a QSO with K3LR at noise level only in the second
SOAPBOX: night, where the conditions to US were worse than the first night.
SOAPBOX: Pity the SV9 stations calling and calling and calling but
SOAPBOX: making very few QSOs. SV9 is another mult we normally miss.
SOAPBOX: Heared also SV5DKL (but we didn't break the pileup), then
SOAPBOX: turned out the caller was a pirate, in fact Satish wrote on
SOAPBOX: FB he didn't operate in the contest.
SOAPBOX: In general it was tough staying awake, with a rate of 5-10 Q/h
SOAPBOX: for some hours.
SOAPBOX: We left the competition 1 hour early, and I am sure we didn't
SOAPBOX: lose that much.
SOAPBOX: Hope for a better CQWW160 in 2027!
SOAPBOX: Thanks for QSOs, 73's
SOAPBOX: Luca IK2PFL
